WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.270
What’s the best way to get my email read?

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.860
How should I send files?

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:12.040
You may have many questions about email conduct
- and we’re here to answer them.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:19.940
A clear subject line can be the difference
between your email being read and being ignored.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:25.400
Professionals are busy people! Subject lines should be clear, short

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.600
and summarise the important part of your message.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.800
For example, if you're emailing your manager 
to request a holiday,

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:40.960
your subject line could be something like
‘holiday request: 10 - 14 August.’

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:48.200
Precise information like project titles, meeting
locations, or your email purpose

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.360
all make good subject lines.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:58.460
Never leave it blank, as it can look careless
and gives the reader no idea what your message

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.300
is about.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.080
In addition to using the subject line, you
can also show that an email is important by

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.100
marking it as urgent or high priority.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:14.320
Not all email programmes have this function,
however.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:20.299
Marking an email as urgent will probably get
it read quicker, but only do so when it is

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:21.299
actually urgent.

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:30.470
For example, a happy birthday email to a co-worker
probably doesn’t require immediate attention,

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:34.500
even if you really love birthdays.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.790
Emails are a great way to send and receive files.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:45.689
However, you should be careful about sending
large files as attachments, or lots of attachments

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:47.200
in one email.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:54.090
Big attachments can fill up the reader’s
email inbox and cause problems for them.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:59.490
If you need to send a big file to someone,
then it is a good idea to send them a download

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.950
link rather than include it as an attachment.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:08.619
You can also use other programmes to resize
or compress files to make them small enough

00:02:08.619 --> 00:02:11.000
to send by email.

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:16.719
Subscribe to our channel for more videos on
how to improve your English language skills.

